# {{app_title}}

A [Plotly Dash](https://dash.plotly.com) app that charts a CSV file,
scaffolded with [dash-app](https://github.com/budescode/dash-app)
on {{create_date}}.

## Run it

```bash
python -m venv .venv && source .venv/bin/activate   # Windows: .venv\Scripts\activate
pip install -r requirements.txt
python app.py
```

Or with [uv](https://docs.astral.sh/uv/) (reads `pyproject.toml`):

```bash
uv sync
uv run app.py
```

Then open http://127.0.0.1:8050 in your browser.

## Use your own data

1. Drop your CSV into `data/` (or replace `sample.csv`)
2. In `app.py`, update `DATA_FILE` and the column names
   (`date`, `region`, `sales`) to match your file
3. Restart the app

## Project layout

| Path               | Purpose                                               |
| ------------------ | ----------------------------------------------------- |
| `app.py`           | Loads the CSV, layout + callback                      |
| `data/sample.csv`  | Sample data, replace with your own                   |
| `assets/`          | CSS/JS files here are auto-loaded by Dash, no config |
| `requirements.txt` | Python dependencies (pip)                             |
| `pyproject.toml`   | Same deps + metadata (uv, poetry)                     |

## Deploy

**Plotly Cloud**, the official hosting, free tier available:

```bash
pip install "dash[cloud]"
plotly user login
plotly app publish
```

The first publish creates a `plotly-cloud.toml` here; commit it, so future
publishes update the same app. Re-publish anytime with `plotly app publish`.

**Any WSGI host**: `app.py` exposes `server = app.server`:

```bash
pip install gunicorn
gunicorn app:server
```
